---
kind: lore
id: puzzle.boiler
title: The boiler and the furnace
---

<beat id="levers" on="examine" target="fixture.boilerLevers" priority="10" spentBy="run.power">
  @narrator: Three levers. Stencilled under the panel, half scraped away: ORDER OF FIRING.
  @nell{mono when="entry.roster.read"}: The roster. Two before one, and never three with the pressure up.
  <branch id="order" prompt="Which order?">
    <choice id="twoOne" label="II, then I">
      @narrator: A thump, a roar, and the boiler catches. Upstairs, all at once, the ward's lights come on in a long stutter, corridor by corridor, like someone running through the building flicking switches.
      ::set{run.power = true}
      @nell{mono}: Everything's awake now. Everything.
      ::lure{room="boiler"}
    </choice>
    <choice id="oneTwo" label="I, then II">
      @narrator: The boiler coughs, shudders, and goes quiet. The needle drops to nothing.
      ::fright
    </choice>
    <choice id="three" label="III first">
      @narrator: The pressure valve does not open. The gauge glass does.
      @narrator: The last thing you see is steam coming for you like a white sheet thrown over a bed.
      ::set{run.fate = "burned"}
      ::set{user.deaths += 1}
      ::end{reason="burned"}
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<beat id="furnace" on="examine" target="fixture.furnace" priority="10" spentBy="holds(burned(ledger))" when="holds(holding(ledger)) && holds(holding(matches))">
  @narrator: The furnace latch is cold. Inside, a grate and forty years of ash.
  <branch id="burn" prompt="The admissions ledger is heavy in your bag.">
    <choice id="burn" label="Burn the ledger">
      @narrator: The first match goes out. The second takes. The pages curl one by one and every name on them blackens and lifts and goes up the flue.
      @child{os}: Thank you, nurse.
      ::consume{item="ledger"}
      ::assert{burned(ledger)}
    </choice>
    <choice id="keep" label="Not yet">
      @nell{mono}: Not yet. If I burn it I can't read it.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>
